    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "type": "grammar",
      "label": "Grammar",
      "title": "Three imperative forms",
      "story": [
        "<b>Sie</b>: infinitive, then Sie. This is the form for patients. <b>Trinken Sie</b> Wasser.",
        "<b>du</b>: the stem. Drop -e when it sounds fine: <b>Trink</b>. Keep -e after -t/-d or irregular: <b>Atme</b>, and learn <b>Nimm</b>, <b>Sieh</b>.",
        "<b>ihr</b>: same as the ihr present, pronoun optional. <b>Trinkt</b> Wasser."
      ],
      "tables": [
        {
          "title": "trinken · nehmen · aufstehen",
          "columns": [
